# Full end-to-end QEMU coverage of the installer chain (spec-install umbrella).
#
# Drives internal/le/qemu/install.go, which builds the installer
# initrd + a credential-matched gokrazy image from scratch, serves them over
# HTTP, boots the installer kernel+initrd in QEMU against a blank disk, asserts
# the initrd's serial success markers, then re-boots the written disk and logs
# in over SSH as the power user (install AC-10 / loadZefsUsers regression).
#
# The installer kernel is operator-supplied by design (ze ships none), so the
# driver self-skips with a clear reason when QEMU, a suitable kernel
# (ZE_INSTALL_KERNEL), a static busybox, or the image-build tooling is absent.
# It exits 0 in both the PASS and SKIP cases; a genuine boot/install/SSH failure
# exits non-zero. The exhaustive path is `./le qemu install-test`.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=./le qemu install-test
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:regex=INSTALL-QEMU: (PASS|SKIP)
